  'site.read.kicker': 'How',
  'site.read.title': 'How to use it.',
  'site.read.p1': "Home is the front. It tells you what is left today. Today is the tap. One question. Did or Not yet. Finish today and the streak goes up. Come back tomorrow.",
  'site.read.p2': "A question can wait until a clock time. Coming up shows the next days so a waiting question is not a blank screen. Last time is yesterday, or the last due day, if you missed it. Late still counts.",
  'site.read.p3': "Add a question from Questions, or start from What to ask. It can be every day, some weekdays, monthly, every few days, or once. The day folds at the hour in Settings, so a 1:00 AM tap still belongs to yesterday if the fold is 4.",
  'site.read.p4':
    'This phone keeps your questions. There is no email. Settings has a copy of the file, an optional number lock, and reminders. Chrome and Android can ping at the ask-after hour. An iPhone can install the page. Pings there are weak until a Mac builds the native app.',
  'site.read.p5': "y or space is Did. s is Not yet. n adds a question. Escape closes a plate. u undoes the last tap for a few seconds.",
