  'help.questions': 'Questions and folders',
  'help.questionsP': "Tap Add on Questions, or Add in the menu. Pick every day or some days, and a time if you want a reminder. Folders group your questions. The ALL chip on Home and Questions filters by folder and by topic.",
  'help.questionsGo': 'See your questions',
  'help.pings': 'Reminders',
  'help.pingsP':
    'Turn on notifications and a question can remind you at its time. Friends, family, cheers and Did we can send you one too. Pick which kinds you get under Settings, and turn on "Hide what it says" to keep questions off your lock screen.',
  'help.pingsGo': 'Notification settings',
  'help.widget': 'Home screen widget',
  'help.widgetP': "Add the Did I widget from your home screen. It shows the next question, and Did and Not yet work right on it. If you are on a Did we, it shows who you are waiting on.",
  'help.people': 'Friends and family',
  'help.peopleP': "Add a friend by their friend ID, or send an invite link. A family shares a folder: anyone can add to it, and a parent can put a question on one person. Send a Did you to ask about something, once or every day; it waits in their inbox until they keep it. Or send a cheer to cheer them on. Friends who join with your code earn you gems, the Night look, and at 15 and 20 friends a buddy and a frame you cannot buy.",
  'help.peopleGo': 'Friends and family',
  'help.we': 'Did we',
  'help.weP1':"A question you answer with someone else. On Add, tap \"Did I\" and pick Did we, then pick friends or family. They say yes to join. Pick when it counts: everyone says did, anyone does, most do, or you take turns a day each. Your Did we’s live in Friends and family, and once your own questions are done they come up on Today to swipe.",
  'help.weP2':"The person who makes it picks what others see: every answer, only who is still waiting, or just a count. Tap the faces to see everyone on it. Days done together build a shared streak that pays coins at 7, 30, 100 and 365 days. Leave any time; your past answers stay. If someone bothers you, Report blocks them and takes you off the cards you share.",
  'help.weGo': 'Start a Did we',
  'help.cheers': 'Cheers',
  "help.cheersP": "A cheer plays on your screen when you finish today, and on everyone’s when a Did we is done together. Get more in the shop and send one to a friend.",
  'help.coins': 'Coins and gems',
  "help.coinsP": "Coins come from answering each day and from shared streaks. Gems come each week, from inviting people, or you can buy them. Spend both in the shop on looks, cheers, buddies, accessories and frames.",
  "help.shopGo": "Open the shop",
  'legal.privacy.together.title': 'Did we, repeats, and reports',
  'legal.privacy.together.body': "Did we. When you start or join a shared question, the others on it see your display name, your buddy (the one you wear from the shop), whether you have joined, and your answers for each day, as far as the card’s owner allows: every answer, only who is still waiting, or just a count. They also see the question, its schedule, and the shared streak. We store the card, who was asked and when, answers, nudges, and when an ask was turned down, so the same ask cannot come straight back.\n\nRepeating Did you’s. A Did you can ask to repeat (every day or some days). It always waits in your inbox until you keep it, even from family. Once kept, it is a question on your own shelf that you can change or remove.\n\nReport and block. Reporting a Did we or a Did you stores a report with the question and blocks that person: you leave cards you share, and their asks and Did you’s stop. They are not told. Nobody reviews reports one by one; blocking is what protects you. We may look at reports if something is brought to us.\n\nLimits. To stop pestering, the servers cap new cards, nudges, repeating Did you’s, and reports per person per day.",
